cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Easy-EO: chainable raster analysis for Earth Observation in Python"
abstract: >-
  A Python library for raster-based Earth Observation analysis. Everything
  happens through a single dataset object that can be clipped, reprojected,
  resampled, reduced to a spectral index or plotted, with each operation
  returning another dataset so an analysis chains as a sequence of steps. A
  search against any SpatioTemporal Asset Catalog returns matching scenes, and
  loading one reads only the pixels covering the area of interest, so imagery
  can be worked on without downloading the scenes it comes from.
authors:
